  ],
  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "For strength path Immortal Gu such as these, Fang Yuan’s strength path dao marks can resonate so he unleashes more than the Gu’s base power.",
        "chapters": [
          758
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "dao-mark-resonance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In Hu Immortal blessed land, Fang Yuan activates the Gu and lifts Dang Hun Mountain with a formless force.",
        "chapters": [
          769
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "dao-mark-resonance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
          "loc_dang_hun_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Strength path dao marks on his body resonate with the Gu;",
        "chapters": [
          758
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "dao-mark-resonance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "the Gu’s own power does not change, but that resonance lets him bring out close to twenty percent more strength in the test.",
        "chapters": [
          769
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "dao-mark-resonance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "While using Pulling Mountain’s eight strength path giant hands to pull the ruin bat’s corpse mountain, Fang Yuan notices Old Lord Can Yang’s life chasing fire has spread into the one hundred and sixty thousand strength path phantoms powering the hands, and wills the phantoms to collapse, dropping the mountain. Forcibly halting Pulling Mountain this way gives him an intense backlash of dizziness and nausea that nearly makes him fall from the air.",
        "chapters": [
          791
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "backlash-from-forcing-a-halt",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_old_lord_can_yang"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "With the Gu he can drag Dang Hun Mountain into his immortal aperture alone.",
        "chapters": [
          1096
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "target-scope",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In Hei Fan grotto-heaven, Fang Yuan uses the Gu to dig out and transplant the entire hibiscus stalactite cave into Mini Southern Border, work that would otherwise have been hard to manage.",
        "chapters": [
          1133
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "target-scope",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_hei_fan_grotto_heaven",
          "loc_mini_southern_border"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Against City Well, Pulling Mountain alone only shakes the well slightly, because City Well is not a mountain even though it sits on the ground and needs earth qi.",
        "chapters": [
          1158
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "target-scope",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_city_well"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan uses Pulling Mountain to move Five Light Mountain out of Liu Qing Yu’s blessed land and into his sovereign immortal aperture, placing it in Mini Southern Border, where it becomes the biggest mountain of them all and pushes Immortal Succession Mountain down to second tallest. Ying Wu Xie cannot move the mountain himself because he no longer holds Pulling Mountain, having once owned it before it was sold to Fang Yuan in those dealings.",
        "chapters": [
          1152
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "moving-five-light-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_five_light_mountain",
          "loc_qing_yu_blessed_land",
          "loc_immortal_succession_mountain",
          "char_ying_wu_xie"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After plundering Frosty Peak’s frost jades, Fang Yuan considers using Pulling Mountain to pull the whole peak into his sovereign blessed land, then decides against it. Acting under his Wu Yi Hai identity, he judges that pulling the mountain would expose his true identity and go beyond what he could justify to Wu clan after already profiting from the affair.",
        "chapters": [
          1312
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "frosty-peak-declined",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_frosty_peak",
          "char_wu_yi_hai",
          "fac_wu_clan"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
